# Three.js Geometry to OBJ Export

## Overview
Exporting Three.js meshes to Wavefront OBJ format requires converting BufferGeometry vertex/face data into the OBJ text format, while applying the mesh's world transformation.

## OBJ File Format Basics
```
# Comment
v x y z          # vertex position
vn nx ny nz      # vertex normal
f v1 v2 v3       # face (1-indexed vertex indices)
f v1//n1 v2//n2  # face with normals
```

## Using OBJExporter (three/addons)

### Installation
```bash
npm install three
```

### Usage with OBJExporter
```javascript
import { OBJExporter } from 'three/addons/exporters/OBJExporter.js';
// or: import { OBJExporter } from 'three/examples/jsm/exporters/OBJExporter.js';

const exporter = new OBJExporter();

// Export a single mesh or group
const objString = exporter.parse(mesh);

// Write to file
fs.writeFileSync('output.obj', objString);
```

### Important Notes
- `OBJExporter.parse()` applies the object's world matrix, so ensure `updateMatrixWorld(true)` is called first.
- It handles `BufferGeometry` with indexed and non-indexed variants.

## Manual OBJ Generation (without OBJExporter)
If OBJExporter is unavailable, you can manually construct the OBJ string:

```javascript
function geometryToOBJ(geometry, worldMatrix) {
    const pos = geometry.getAttribute('position');
    const normal = geometry.getAttribute('normal');
    const index = geometry.getIndex();

    let obj = '';
    const tempVec = new THREE.Vector3();
    const normalMatrix = new THREE.Matrix3().getNormalMatrix(worldMatrix);

    // Vertices
    for (let i = 0; i < pos.count; i++) {
        tempVec.set(pos.getX(i), pos.getY(i), pos.getZ(i));
        tempVec.applyMatrix4(worldMatrix);
        obj += `v ${tempVec.x} ${tempVec.y} ${tempVec.z}\n`;
    }

    // Normals
    if (normal) {
        for (let i = 0; i < normal.count; i++) {
            tempVec.set(normal.getX(i), normal.getY(i), normal.getZ(i));
            tempVec.applyMatrix3(normalMatrix).normalize();
            obj += `vn ${tempVec.x} ${tempVec.y} ${tempVec.z}\n`;
        }
    }

    // Faces (OBJ is 1-indexed)
    if (index) {
        for (let i = 0; i < index.count; i += 3) {
            const a = index.getX(i) + 1;
            const b = index.getX(i + 1) + 1;
            const c = index.getX(i + 2) + 1;
            if (normal) {
                obj += `f ${a}//${a} ${b}//${b} ${c}//${c}\n`;
            } else {
                obj += `f ${a} ${b} ${c}\n`;
            }
        }
    } else {
        for (let i = 0; i < pos.count; i += 3) {
            const a = i + 1, b = i + 2, c = i + 3;
            obj += `f ${a} ${b} ${c}\n`;
        }
    }

    return obj;
}
```

## Applying World Transforms
Critical for correct export when meshes have local transforms:
```javascript
root.updateMatrixWorld(true);
const worldMatrix = mesh.matrixWorld.clone();
